<!-- Build-menu placement (owner 2026-10-11, ruling #4: "Our tanks should go where other storage tanks go. Our pipes/hoses/
     wires/conduit should go where those normally go."). Vanilla has no liquid pipes; the Vanilla Expanded pipe mods (Chemfuel,
     Helixien Gas, Nutrient Paste: VCHE_ChemfuelPipe, PS_ChemfuelTank, VNPE_NutrientPastePipe, VNPE_NutrientPasteVat ...) put
     pipes, valves AND tanks in one "pipe networks" tab, and EACH of those mods ships this identical DesignationCategoryDef so the
     tab exists whichever of them is loaded. FlowWorks follows the same convention and ships it too: with any VE pipe mod loaded
     our pipe, tanks, hose reel and adapters sit beside theirs; without one, the tab is ours alone. Copied verbatim from
     Vanilla Chemfuel Expanded 1.6/Defs/Designation.xml (workshop 2792917473), read 2026-10-11. Dubs Bad Hygiene uses its own
     Hygiene tab for water plumbing only (water towers, sewage), so it is not the convention for any-liquid pipes. -->
<Defs>
  <DesignationCategoryDef>
    <defName>VCHE_PipeNetworks</defName>
    <label>pipe networks</label>
    <order>350</order>
    <specialDesignatorClasses>
      <li>Designator_Cancel</li>
      <li>Designator_Deconstruct</li>
    </specialDesignatorClasses>
  </DesignationCategoryDef>
</Defs>
